Fujifilm X100VI (04cb:0305): declare capture and preview (PTP_CAP|PTP_CAP_PREVIEW), like the X-T5 / X-H2 / X-M5 rows.
2.5.34 and master have the row at 0 ("no capture", from github issue 964) — but the X100VI supports USB tethered
shooting (SET UP > CONNECTION SETTING > CONNECTION MODE > USB TETHER SHOOTING AUTO / FIXED; Fujifilm lists it for
X Acquire and Capture One), and the Fuji capture path of the ptp2 camlib (camera_fuji_capture, PriorityMode 0xd207,
events patch) is the same one Prism measured on the GFX 100S (30/09/2026). Measured in Prism on Leo's X100VI
(01/10/2026): with the row at 0 libgphoto2 offers only download + the camera's own shutter; the flags are what gate
gp_camera_capture / gp_camera_capture_preview for the body. Remove when upstream sets the flags itself.
--- a/camlibs/ptp2/library.c
+++ b/camlibs/ptp2/library.c
@@ -2751,7 +2751,7 @@
 	/* via email */
 	{"Fuji:Fujifilm GFX100 II",		0x04cb, 0x02fe, PTP_CAP|PTP_CAP_PREVIEW},
 	/* https://github.com/gphoto/libgphoto2/issues/964 */
-	{"Fuji:Fujifilm X100VI",		0x04cb, 0x0305, 0},
+	{"Fuji:Fujifilm X100VI",		0x04cb, 0x0305, PTP_CAP|PTP_CAP_PREVIEW},
 	/* Capture when camera set in Tether. */
 	{"Fuji:Fujifilm X-M5",			0x04cb, 0x030c, PTP_CAP|PTP_CAP_PREVIEW},
 	/* No capture support. */
